  "facts": [
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F01",
      "statement": "Follow the maintenance timetable in the vehicle’s manual to reduce mechanical-failure risk.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 277,
          "char_end_exclusive": 469,
          "excerpt": "You should follow the recommended \nmaintenance schedule listed in the vehicle owner’s manual.  Following these preventive measures greatly \nreduces the chance your vehicle will have a problem.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "ffef036a8e5c485271d1b62f895741124594db1b53a44c019100d79fea45cf19"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F02",
      "statement": "For brakes that stop working, the manual first instructs repeated pedal pumping, which may restore enough pressure to stop.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 567,
          "char_end_exclusive": 595,
          "excerpt": "If your brakes stop working:",
          "excerpt_sha256": "2325f3fc4b976329912948cebd1c417246368e81090d5bc6a2fad7ca02eaae39"
        },
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 599,
          "char_end_exclusive": 704,
          "excerpt": "Pump the brake pedal several times. This will often build up enough brake pressure to allow you \nto stop.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "c3d0aa5e99facd305b9bfde630e08b2d41ca1f1cc9dcd4f23ff2426a6f1993b0"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F03",
      "statement": "If pumping failed brakes does not help, the source next calls for gradual use of the parking-brake handle to avoid rear-wheel lock and a skid.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 708,
          "char_end_exclusive": 850,
          "excerpt": "If that does not work, use the parking brake.  Pull on the parking brake handle slowly so you will \nnot lock the rear wheels and cause a skid.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "c82c1f2562850731feaae0ecf9b7fd6bb314a1937393475dd12e8d5851caed87"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F04",
      "statement": "If the parking-brake attempt starts a skid, be prepared to release it.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 852,
          "char_end_exclusive": 917,
          "excerpt": "Be ready to release the brake if the vehicle does start to \nskid.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "99e0c0f468c1429683e5f1ab5a2a7242999f2648d1b24f640927d18b04b95656"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F05",
      "statement": "If those brake-failure measures fail, the manual next directs downshifting and finding a safe place to slow and stop off the roadway.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 921,
          "char_end_exclusive": 1062,
          "excerpt": "If that does not work, start shifting to lower gears and look for a safe place to slow to a stop.  \nMake sure the vehicle is off the roadway.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "abbf0bef6979b8acb256d4023bc63123a1c97124dc8c00839c617a93b8211968"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F06",
      "statement": "Do not continue driving a vehicle that has no working brakes.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 1064,
          "char_end_exclusive": 1104,
          "excerpt": "Do not drive the vehicle without brakes.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "3c5836c39a032d04d5b772305de5b5bbe6fdca023a98e53c7841aee05f0cfe44"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F07",
      "statement": "For a sudden tire deflation, grip the wheel firmly and maintain a straight course.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 1122,
          "char_end_exclusive": 1151,
          "excerpt": "If a tire suddenly goes flat:",
          "excerpt_sha256": "98f130541379285fa1996a3c205528000398f31232a80de5660eaec0cdf198cc"
        },
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 1155,
          "char_end_exclusive": 1223,
          "excerpt": "Hold the steering wheel tightly and keep the vehicle going straight.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "a86c0efbe6b2339c0ab691d32206fce9505a180034ac9f45ba80a8524e6cb9e0"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F08",
      "statement": "The blowout procedure calls for gradual slowing by releasing the accelerator and braking lightly.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
          "page_text_sha256": "ac89ea8f0b5f1f133d50937189000c205cf962e616df31f04e0b46e977c47ed4",
          "char_start": 1227,
          "char_end_exclusive": 1309,
          "excerpt": "Slow down gradually.  Take your foot off the gas pedal and use the brakes lightly.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "e6e8f31a2885781dd8aca809d87547988c0babc84c307a1f5a53a254e3d5034a"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C",
      "fact_id": "sec14-F09",
      "statement": "After a blowout, avoid stopping in the roadway if possible and move to a safe place off the road.",
      "primary_physical_page": 34,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 34,
