          "char_start": 532,
          "char_end_exclusive": 638,
          "excerpt": "Stay off the brake.  Until the vehicle slows, your brakes will not work and \ncould cause you to skid more.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "39f1253e0506c92b0e649ad95d02eef631768373301bb24814ccca7fce362e83"
        }
      ],
      "independent_audit": false,
      "current_source_currency_verified": false
    },
    {
      "section": "sec14",
      "part": "C2",
      "fact_id": "sec14-R19",
      "statement": "During a skid, steer toward the desired travel direction; as the vehicle straightens, correct the wheel back to avoid a skid the other way.",
      "primary_physical_page": 36,
      "supporting_physical_pages": [],
      "verdict": "SOURCE_FIDELITY_CHECKED_BY_AUTHOR",
      "conditions_actors_numbers_reviewed": true,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "physical_page": 36,
          "page_text_sha256": "c2ec9c5e435f517184524d185e187c43e228227d8cacf5cf1515bd3cd114bc12",
          "char_start": 648,
          "char_end_exclusive": 920,
          "excerpt": "Turn the steering wheel in the direction you want the vehicle to go.  As \nsoon as the vehicle begins to straighten out, turn the steering wheel back the \nother way.  If you do not do so, your vehicle may swing around in the other \ndirection and you could start a new skid.",
          "excerpt_sha256": "03436a4bf84a082b95a2d668256b5302aae3bf5d9fe179cf88f58337be0107b2"
